\pard\b\f0\fs24 Storm Rail\b0\f1\fs18\par
\par
\b\f0 Round capacity:\b0\f1  Variable by load and platform; exact handheld capacity not stated.\par
\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  Heavy anti-material and anti-systems weapon built for rogue AI, used both as a shoulder-carried weapon and as a mounted ship cannon.\par
\b\f0 Proficient Characters:\b0\f1  Tao Vang, Tex Kovachnikov, John Walker.\par
\b\f0 Season:\b0\f1  Chapters 1-4.\par
\b\f0 Unique Features:\b0\f1  Two EMP modes, kinetic rail mode for metal slugs, Mark IV shoulder-mount compatibility, and derivatives large enough to serve as ship-mounted storm rail cannons.\par
\b\f0 Description:\b0\f1  The Storm Rail was developed in response to fears of rogue AI compromising human systems. Its EMP settings can either overwhelm electronics or target operating frequencies with more controlled disruption. If that fails, the weapon switches to brute-force kinetic rail fire.\par
\b\f0 Sights:\b0\f1  Precision-cut carry case, heavy shoulder clamp, bright charging lines and a barrel built like a personal cannon.\par
\b\f0 Sounds:\b0\f1  Coils rising, electronic whine and a hard concussive clap on discharge.\par
\b\f0 Smell:\b0\f1  Ozone, hot metal and scorched air around the coils.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  Tau introduces it in training, Tex later uses it as a decisive anti-drone weapon, and the Beverly mounts a larger storm rail variant.\par
\b\f0 Built at:\b0\f1  Protectant rail-weapons program drawing on older orbital rail technology.\par
}
